{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475455-questions-about-the-himalayan-wars","id":1475455,"title":"Questions about the Himalayan wars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-25T08:26:50-08:00","id":1475455,"title":"Questions about the Himalayan wars","content":"From what I've learned the Himalayan wars lasted 600 years. It went on for a long time, most likely due to the the factions involved in this war continuously reincarnating with their memories after they were killed.<br /> <br /> Now I know there was a lot of anti surveillance magic being used to stop any sort of scrying, so there's probably not too much that is well known about this time.<br /> <br /> How do the other factions like the traditions, technocracy, krafts, and the such view this war?<br /> <br /> If member of both the factions that were involved were able to reincarnate to continue fighting in the war, why was voormas so afraid to die? Couldn't he just reincarnate?<br /> <br /> Are there any mages running around who remember the the war?<br /> <br /> If reincarnation is possible, why don't more mages do it? Other than their belief of course<br /> <br /> Here's the link for the wiki-<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Himalayan_Wars\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Himalayan_Wars</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 02-25-2022, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T09:35:12-08:00","id":1475456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475455-questions-about-the-himalayan-wars#post1475455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any mages running around who remember the the war?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can recall Nu Ying, Akashic major character. He can remember every lifetime back to the Himalayan Wars.<br /> <br /> Wiki: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nu_Ying\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nu_Ying</a><br /> <br /> More can be found on 2nd Tradition book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T11:27:24-08:00","id":1475459,"title":"","content":"To respond a bit to the point about Voormas:<br /> <br /> 1) Reincarnation is not a perfect solution, because it is possible to stop it from happening. A Mage that receives Gilgul, for example, will not be able to magically reincarnate themselves because their Avatar, the source of their power, has been destroyed. Even if the situation is extremely unlikely, it is possible, and fears are not going to be perfectly rational.<br /> <br /> 2) Voormas was afraid of more than his personal death, that could be overcome through reincarnation. To quote the wiki for a moment (not a perfect source, but I'm fairly certain this is just an abridged version of something copied straight out the text):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Wolf Wiki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Voormas served the gods for centuries, always testing himself to conquer his fear of the afterlife \u2013 a sliver of bad faith that dogged him while he used the skulls of priests as begging bowls. The Euthanatos confused his fervor with genuine faith. Voormas became a talented death mage, but his fear remained and was intensified by his growing understanding of the Wheel. Something was wrong with the cosmos; karma was more apt to punish than reward. Each turn of the Wheel was thicker with chaos. A lesser mage would have been satisfied with life-extending spells, but the Grand Harvester knew that those mages were simply bulwark against ultimate destruction. He had to throw down the Cycle and steal the thrones of the gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Voormas was afraid of the larger idea that the cycle of life and death itself was broken in an irreparable way, that the multiverse was inevitably spiraling down the drain towards unavoidable entropy. Obviously Voormas had avoided death for centuries, but he believed it could not be cheated indefinitely.<br /> <br /> And to an extent, a lot of the text supports that interpretation. Most WoD gamelines include the spectre of some imminent apocalypse or mysterious doom on the horizon, the sort of thing that can't simply be avoided through reincarnating after a (relatively) mundane death. Whether or not you give into despair or have faith in some kind of solution, man-made or divine, is a recurring theme throughout the series. Voormas simply didn't have faith in any solution other than trying to stop the entire process through brute force, as the quote above indicates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T11:48:17-08:00","id":1475460,"title":"","content":"These answers make sense, Thanks!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T12:24:14-08:00","id":1475461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475455-questions-about-the-himalayan-wars#post1475455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If reincarnation is possible, why don't more mages do it? Other than their belief of course</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's heavily suggested at various points that they do. They just don't remember to varying degrees.<br /> <br /> However, it's a bit more complicated, because it's the avatar that gets reincarnated. So whilst certain people can remember the past deeds of their avatar, there's still a heavy disconnect between the person today, and the person the avatar was previously attached to. Like, even Akashics don't immediately remember, and have to live a different life until they Awaken. Which leads to...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It went on for a long time, most likely due to the the factions involved in this war continuously reincarnating with their memories after they were killed. </div> </div> </div>It's not stated, but that might be in part because it takes time to reincarnate. Like, Tradition Book: Akashic Brotherhood has a flashback to the Himalayan War that includes a newly awakened Akashic who's about 12 or 13 (and who has started murdering Euthanatos she remembers as enemies from her past lives). If you consider that the Awakened are very rare, there would have been pretty long stretches of inaction as the two sides grow up again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-25T15:29:06-08:00","id":1475470,"title":"","content":"Wont enough levels in mind help you regain memories quicker?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-26T15:57:57-08:00","id":1475507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475455-questions-about-the-himalayan-wars?p=1475470#post1475470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wont enough levels in mind help you regain memories quicker?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't see why not. Mind that the Akashics at least seem to think you should (or possibly need to) do it on your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-27T00:06:11-08:00","id":1475522,"title":"","content":"Also bear in mind that some of the Akashics' opponents could attack memories (including the Akashic Record itself) and philosophical concepts with their magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T21:56:30-08:00","id":1475711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475455-questions-about-the-himalayan-wars#post1475455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do the other factions like the traditions, technocracy, krafts, and the such view this war?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most don't think much about it, because the war was a really long time ago. Those are among the oldest Traditions to take a form we can recognize today, the war happened at a time and place with little significance to everyone else.<br /> <br /> It isn't that they don't know about the war (although most probably don't, as it is an obscure historical curiosity), but that its main impact in anything today is the very state of those two Traditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475455-questions-about-the-himalayan-wars#post1475455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If member of both the factions that were involved were able to reincarnate to continue fighting in the war, why was voormas so afraid to die? Couldn't he just reincarnate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reincarnation isn't immortality. You suffer death, goes to the beyond, stays there an unknown amount of time, then returns, starts life anew as a newborn without memories, without a say on when, where or from whom you will be born, to only after Awakening (it can be immediately, it isn't always so) some memories coming back. Memories, not dots, just memories.<br /> <br /> You can skew things in your favor with magic, but there are too many variables to deal with, many successes needed and risks in even trying that can not simply mess with your current predicament, but with your entire future, defenseless incarnation. Even then, you can hardly say that the new incarnation is the exact same person on every meaningful way, just be in peace with how much it can be so (or, for Voormas, not be in peace with it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475455-questions-about-the-himalayan-wars#post1475455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any mages running around who remember the the war?</div> </div> </div> </div>Plenty, actually, although very few remember big chunks of it. Some even continue it at their own discretion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475455-questions-about-the-himalayan-wars#post1475455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If reincarnation is possible, why don't more mages do it? Other than their belief of course</div> </div> </div> </div>They all do. Those two Traditions have just a stronger link to the idea, but they all do, even the Techies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T15:35:08-08:00","id":1475748,"title":"","content":"What's fun with reincarnation is to have a character who was part of the enemy faction during their past life. They awaken and develop strong personal ties to current in-faction Mages before their memories surface.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}